This is a spice folder that xyce will run in
That's why it has the sky130 PDK and all the extracted/behavioral spice files. The modified PDK is at combined (/usr/local/share/pdk/sky130A/libs.tech/combined in a normal instalation). The extracted/behavioral files are in ext/.

The output file will also show up in here.

The device model path has been modified to be relative to this directory.

From xschem, the spice netlist has to be generated in this directory. Running from xschem won't work. You need to make a cli at this directory and run manually with the xyce tool.

EDITS AFTER GENERATION:

The line:
.lib /usr/local/share/pdk/sky130A/libs.tech/combined/sky130.lib.spice tt
Should be:
.lib share/pdk/sky130A/libs.tech/combined/sky130.lib.spice tt

This directory is about 8 gigs. so not very light. There's a limit of 50 gigs when using the supercomputer workspace.

